<decompilertest>
<!--
    GH-839 (kuna): "clang -O2: a variadic tail call after push %rax/pop %rcx
    gains the popped rcx and rdx as arguments"
    https://github.com/Noelo-Lab/kuna/issues/839
    Image (x86-64, linked flat at 0x100000; the callees pr, h, g, hl, q6, init,
    use, use3 and __printf_chk are symbols with no bytes):
      clang 14 -O2 of
        int a2(int k) { return pr("%d", h(k)); }
        int a3(int k) { return pr("%f", g(k)); }
        int a4(int k, int x, int y) { return pr("%d %d %d", h(k), x, y); }
        long sp6(long a,long b,long c,long d,long e,long f) {
          long r = hl(a); long s = hl(r); long t = q6(r, b, c, d, e, f);
          return t + q6(s, a, b, c, d, e) + f; }
      hand-assembled
        a5: push %rax; call h; ...; pop %r8; jmp pr   (the slot comes back in r8)
        a6: push %rax; mov %rsp,%rdi; call init; ...; pop %rdx; jmp pr
      gcc 11 -O2 -fno-omit-frame-pointer of
        void fa1(void){ use(__builtin_frame_address(1)); }
        void fa2(int k){ printf("%d %p\n", k, __builtin_frame_address(1)); }
        void fa3(void){ use3(__builtin_frame_address(0),
                             __builtin_frame_address(1), __builtin_return_address(0)); }
        void fa4(void){ void *p = __builtin_frame_address(1); use(0); use(p); }
      hand-assembled (q declared long q(long a, ...))
        q:  lea 1(%rcx),%rax; ret
        f1: push %rax; call h; mov $10,%ecx; pop %rdx; jmp q
        f4: the same with call q; add $1,%rax; ret
    Stage model: P4 call recovery, input-trial scoring.  clang keeps the stack
    aligned around the one call with push %rax and takes the slot back with
    pop %rcx before the variadic tail call.  ActionActiveParam scores the
    register trials before the stack is heritaged, so rcx is a raw LOAD that
    the ancestor walk took as solid movement; the trial went active and
    fillinMap filled rdx in below it.  The slot only gives back the caller's
    incoming rax, which no prototype passes.  `option reloadarg` re-traces
    such a trial once the frame is heritaged.
    Pass 1 (default, reloadarg on) and pass 2 (reloadarg off):
    #1/#2: pass 1 prints a2, a5 and a3 with the format and the one value.
    #3: pass 2 reproduces the bug: pr("%d",(uint8)v1,v3,v2).
    #4-#6: a4 keeps its three varargs, sp6 the parameter it reloads into r8,
    a6 the slot init wrote through &slot, in both passes.
    #7-#9: the caller's saved rbp that __builtin_frame_address(1) reads from
    the frame is callee-saved, not scratch: fa1-fa4 keep it in both passes.
    #10: f1/f4 keep the junk rdx because the real rcx argument sits above it.
-->
